<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">survival</ansi>

Every member of your company, you and each companion alike, keeps three
needs: Hunger, Thirst, and Fatigue. Each runs 0 to 100. 100 means fully
fed, watered, or rested; 0 means starving, dehydrated, or collapsed.
These belong to each member individually, not the company as a whole.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">What drains them</ansi>

Nothing drains while you sit idle or log off. Needs only change when
something spends them:

  - Travelling a route (<ansi fg="command">help travel</ansi>) spends Hunger, Thirst, and
    Fatigue over the journey, by however much that route calls for.
  - Walking from room to room off the road costs Fatigue as strain
    (<ansi fg="command">help strain</ansi>); rough or wild ground costs more than a road,
    and settlements cost nothing.
  - Cold costs Fatigue, and heat costs Thirst, while you're exposed to
    it (<ansi fg="command">help temperature</ansi>).

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Bands</ansi>

  <ansi fg="yellow">Value</ansi>    <ansi fg="yellow">Hunger</ansi>    <ansi fg="yellow">Thirst</ansi>       <ansi fg="yellow">Fatigue</ansi>
  76-100   Well fed   Hydrated     Rested
  51-75    Sated      Comfortable  Ready
  26-50    Hungry     Thirsty      Tired
  1-25     Starving   Parched      Exhausted
  0        Starving   Dehydrated   Collapsed

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Running out</ansi>

A member at 0 Fatigue is Collapsed: your company can't set out on a
route until someone rests (<ansi fg="command">help camp</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help inn</ansi>). Anyone above 0
but at or below 25 Fatigue is Exhausted; you'll be told when a member
crosses into or out of either band.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">In battle</ansi>

When a battle begins, each member's needs set its battle condition for
that whole battle (you can't eat mid-fight, so feed the company first):

  <ansi fg="yellow">Need</ansi>      <ansi fg="yellow">Hungry/Thirsty/Tired</ansi>   <ansi fg="yellow">Starving/Parched/Exhausted or worse</ansi>
  Hunger    -5% damage dealt       -10% damage dealt
  Thirst    +5% damage taken       +10% damage taken
  Fatigue   -5 hit chance          -10 hit chance (-20 Collapsed)

Damage counts blows and spells, dealt and taken.
Sated, Comfortable and Ready or better cost nothing. A cooked meal adds
a buff for its next few battles (<ansi fg="command">help cooking</ansi>). The fight opens with a
"Going in:" line naming each member's condition; <ansi fg="command">survival</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">status</ansi>,
<ansi fg="command">conditions</ansi> and the Company panel show it for the next battle, and the
battle screen and Combat tab show the one the fight began with.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Feeding your company</ansi>

<ansi fg="command">eat</ansi> and <ansi fg="command">drink</ansi> restore Hunger and/or Thirst from your own pack, for
yourself or a named companion. See <ansi fg="command">help eat</ansi> and <ansi fg="command">help drink</ansi>.

Rooms with fresh water let you drink for free and refill a waterskin
(<ansi fg="command">drink water</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">fill</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">company fill</ansi>; a waterskin drunk dry stays as an empty one to refill); <ansi fg="command">look</ansi> shows them on its "Here:" line. See
<ansi fg="command">help resources</ansi>. Away from supplies, a company can work for them: herbs, firewood,
fish and game take time and effort (<ansi fg="command">help gathering</ansi>).

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Usage:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">survival</ansi>
  Shows every current company member's Hunger, Thirst, and Fatigue, and
  an "In battle:" line for anyone whose needs or meal change a fight.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help gathering</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help resources</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help eat</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help drink</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help camp</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help inn</ansi>,
<ansi fg="command">help temperature</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help strain</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help travel</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help company</ansi>.

Fatigue's hit chance cut is on physical blows (<ansi fg="command">help battlefield</ansi>).
